                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolutely fantastic point n click series, set in Victorian England inspired by the tales of H P Lovecraft and Edgar Allen Poe. Episodic format works great for adventure games as each self contained episode only has a limited amount of locations and objects, so it's never too hard to work out what to do. Puzzle's are all pretty logical, so you should be fine with no guides for a first playthough, but you'll need another run through with one to get all achievements, the secrets are pretty damn obscure. \r\n\r\nI wasn't a huge fan of the 8bit graphics at first, I usually prefer something between Monkey Island and Broken Sword type pixel art for these type of game's but it works really well here (your imagination filling gaps, just like Lovecraft stories) and use's what it has incredibly artisticly. The story is really fantastic but you'll need the second collection to properly finish it and fully understand it. I am a huge Lovecraft fan and this is one of the more authentic and respectful games of the many games tagged \"Lovecraftian\" so I will have some bias.",
